# tally 2.1.8 item 77 (#201), E §4.1 step 2 and L §4.4: a test of a window-dated movement that comes out one way on
# some of its days and another on the rest is the window's hole, as far as the refusal or the other class would reach.
# st covers konto from 03-01 to 03-07, so pay, dated in window(03-05, 03-10) and before K (03-08) only on its first
# three days, is modelled past on those days (open: no observation) and booked as past on the rest: c1 and c3 are the
# hole, and each splits. As known 2026-03-07, st isn't known and nothing is covered (c5). 2.1.7's refcore asked the
# window's first day (0.00 PLN). The plan's i77b.
# tally 2.2 (2.2-4): the clause `windows each` is cut; its asks are the plain line, the hole with each unknown day it
# carries named (`unknown day:`, 2.2-11). A caller who takes the window as one day pins its cell.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-03-08
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-06-30

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2025-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input bank: observed
input amt: money PLN
input wd: date

move pay: transfers
  on wd
  leg cash from world to konto amount amt

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  amt = 100.00 PLN "s"
  wd = window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-10) "s"
  opening[konto] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"

version st
  cite s
  governs 2026-03-01..2026-03-07
  known 2026-03-08
  covers konto

ask c1: bal(konto, 2026-03-31)
ask c2: bal(konto, 2026-03-31)
ask c3: flows(pay, 2026-03)
ask c4: flows(pay, 2026-03)
ask c5: bal(konto, 2026-03-31) as known 2026-03-07
ask c6: bal(konto, 2026-03-31) as known 2026-03-07
=== expect
c1: ?"date within window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-10) not precise enough for a balance" (pay)
  unknown day: wd
  cut 2026-03-08
c2: ?"date within window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-10) not precise enough for a balance" (pay)
  unknown day: wd
  cut 2026-03-08
c3: ?"date within window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-10) not precise enough for flows of pay" (pay)
  unknown day: wd
  cut 2026-03-08
c4: ?"date within window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-10) not precise enough for flows of pay" (pay)
  unknown day: wd
  cut 2026-03-08
c5: 100.00 PLN
  unfulfilled: pay
  cut 2026-03-07
c6: 100.00 PLN
  unfulfilled: pay
  cut 2026-03-07
